/N 385 0 R
>>
/V (Environmental Monitoring Summary\072\012Personnel monitoring plates for Clea S\056 Garza\054 including left\055 and right\055touch plates\054 showed no microbial growth on the date before testing \05008 May 2026\051\054 the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 and the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051\056\012\012For ISO 5 BSC E001309\054 daily surface sampling of four locations showed no microbial growth on the date before testing \05008 May 2026\051\056 On the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 1 CFU was recovered from S1 associated with Clea S\056 Garza\056 The recovery was documented under ETX\055260518\0550273\073 microbial identification indicated colony\055like artifact \050White\054 shiny\054 hardened\054 smooth area embedded on agar\051\056 Surface sampling performed on the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051 showed no microbial growth\056\012\012Settling sampling of ISO 5 BSC E001309\054 including two locations\054 showed no microbial growth on the date before testing \05008 May 2026\051\054 the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 and the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051\056\012\012Weekly active\055air monitoring of Suite 117 conducted during the week before testing and the week of testing showed no microbial growth\056\012\012Weekly surface monitoring of the anteroom and cleanroom areas associated with Suite 117 showed no microbial growth during the week before testing or the week of testing\056\012\012During the interview\054 the analyst indicated that no obvious abnormalities or deviations occurred during the testing process\056 All materials were disinfected before testing\054 and the relevant cleanroom and ISO 5 BSC were cleaned and prepared before testing in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0552 and MICRO\055SOP\0559\056\012\012Monthly cleaning and disinfection of the cleanroom suite\054 including the ISO 8 anteroom \050117\051\054 ISO 7 buffer room \050117A\051\054 ISO 7 cleanroom \050117B\051\054 and the ISO 5 biosafety cabinets located within Room 117B\054 were performed on 26 April 2026 by Analyst \055 Tamiru Kotisso and Cuong Du \055 in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0559\054 Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\056 All H2O2 indicators passed\054 confirming the successful completion and effectiveness of the monthly cleaning and disinfection activities within Rooms 117\054 117A\054 and 117B\056 Additionally\054 routine cleaning and disinfection were performed before and after the testing activity in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0559\056\012\012It is also important to note that no samples processed by Clea S\056 Garza in ISO 5 BSC E001309 on the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051 failed SCAN RDI testing\056\012\012Based on the available evidence\054 one colony\055like artifact was observed on ScanC\057O CGS E001309 S1 11MAY2026 in ISO 5 BSC E001309 on the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\056 However\054 the observation could not be confirmed as a viable microbial CFU because no growth was obtained following inoculation onto fresh media\056 Therefore\054 the observation may represent a nonviable or non\055microbial artifact\054 including a potential artifact associated with agar preparation or the agar\055pouring process\056\012\012If the observed artifact had represented a viable CFU\054 it would appear to be an isolated event\056 This assessment is supported by the absence of microbial recovery from Clea S\056 Garza\047s personnel\055monitoring plates on the date before testing \05008 May 2026\051\054 the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 and the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051\073 the absence of growth from BSC E001309 surface samples collected on the date before testing and the date after testing\073 and the absence of growth from ISO 5 settling plates throughout the bracketing period\056\012\012The negative ISO 5 settling\054 personnel\054 and bracketing surface monitoring results demonstrate that the BSC E001309 critical environment remained in a state of control\056 The available data do not support migration\054 persistence\054 or recurrence of contamination within ISO 5 BSC E001309\056 Collectively\054 the evidence supports that the recovery was an isolated\054 transient\054 and non\055recurring event\054 while established cleaning\054 disinfection\054 and aseptic controls remained effective\056)
>>
endobj
